Core Problem (let’s be honest)

“I read first 10 lines of the log and asked you”

This is the single most common mid-level developer weakness.

What seniors do differently

They don’t read logs — they hunt causes.

Logs are not news headlines.
They are stack traces, and the root cause is almost never at the top.

🧠 Mental Model You Must Adopt (non-negotiable)
❌ Junior thinking

“App failed → read first error → panic → ask someone”

✅ Senior thinking

“App failed → scroll → find ROOT CAUSE → map to code → verify scope”

You must train your eyes, not your memory.

Naming Pattern Scan (very effective)

Search:

class .*Controller

If you see:

sample.CounterController
test.CounterController

🚨 STOP. You already found a bug.
Maven “bean conflict pre-check” trick

Run with debug condition report:

mvn spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.arguments=--debug

Spring will print:

Which beans are created

Why

From where

This is gold for early detection.

DETECT DUPLICATE BEANS EARLY (AUTOMATIC WAY)
Add this in application.yml (dev only):
spring:
  main:
    allow-bean-definition-overriding: false

👉 This forces Spring to fail FAST
👉 No silent overrides
👉 You immediately see conflicts

(Seniors always keep this disabled)
PREVENT THIS USING SPRING PROFILES (PROFESSIONAL WAY)
@Profile("test")
@RestController
public class CounterController {}
Now it only loads when:
spring.profiles.active=test
